{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01TrASpHrFiB9RGarKnsHAiC", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://ridibooks.com/author/44849\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yi_Hwang\"}, {\"url\": \"https://kbmaeil.com/article/201409110109301\"}, {\"url\": \"https://thewiki.kr/w/이황\"}, {\"url\": \"https://koreanhugo.substack.com/p/the-blacksmiths-path-to-wisdom\"}, {\"url\": \"https://m.cafe.daum.net/SANBANGSAN/H38C/1398\"}, {\"url\": \"https://encykorea.aks.ac.kr/Article/E0065338\"}, {\"url\": \"https://poetrytalks.org/C1130\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.ktriptips.com/kor/tourspot/2772666\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T23:52:04.971Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "이황 단양군수 부임 1548년", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01Ru9NM6ULvG7tTrTB1k5io6", "content": [{"title": "ridibooks.com", "url": "https://ridibooks.com/author/44849"}, {"title": "Yi Hwang", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yi_Hwang"}, {"title": "kbmaeil.com", "url": "https://kbmaeil.com/article/201409110109301"}, {"title": "thewiki.kr", "url": "https://thewiki.kr/w/이황"}, {"title": "Hugo's Study Room", "url": "https://koreanhugo.substack.com/p/the-blacksmiths-path-to-wisdom"}, {"title": "daum.net", "url": "https://m.cafe.daum.net/SANBANGSAN/H38C/1398"}, {"title": "encykorea.aks.ac.kr", "url": "https://encykorea.aks.ac.kr/Article/E0065338"}, {"title": "poetrytalks.org", "url": "https://poetrytalks.org/C1130"}, {"title": "www.ktriptips.com", "url": "https://www.ktriptips.com/kor/tourspot/2772666"}]}, "The search didn't confirm the premise. I found no source saying Yi Hwang (이황) was appointed Danyang magistrate in 1548.\n\n- **Possible mix-up with a disciple:** One result describes a person who was a disciple of Yi Hwang and served as Danyang magistrate the year after 1556, then became Seongju magistrate in 1560. That points to 1557, not 1548. The page doesn't name him in the excerpt, so I can't confirm the name.\n- **Yi Hwang's 1548 post is unconfirmed:** A Korean article mentions his tenure as Punggi magistrate, but the excerpt cuts off, so I can't say from these results what post he held in 1548.\n- **Basic biography:** Yi Hwang lived from 1501 to 1570 and was a Joseon-period Confucian scholar, per the English Wikipedia entry.\n\nTo settle the 1548 question, I'd check the 『명종실록』 or Yi Hwang's biographical chronology (연보) in the 퇴계전서 or the Korean Encyclopedia (한국민족문화대백과사전) entry on 이황, which would list his appointments by year."], "durationSeconds": 7.855305917, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01TrASpHrFiB9RGarKnsHAiC", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
